    <h2>This Website</h2>
    <p>
        This section describes the processing that takes place when you visit
        this website (repeatlab.netlify.app), as distinct from the App.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>No cookies and no consent banner.</strong> This Website does not
        set any cookies, and it does not store or read any information on your device
        (no local storage, no session storage, no device fingerprinting). For this
        reason no cookie consent banner is displayed. Nothing on this Website
        requires your consent under Section 25 of the German Digital Services Data
        Protection Act (TDDDG) or Article 5(3) of the ePrivacy Directive.
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>
            <strong>Server Log Data:</strong> This Website is hosted by Netlify, Inc.
            When you access a page, your browser automatically transmits data that is
            recorded in server log files: your IP address, the date and time of the
            request, the page requested, the referring URL, and your browser and
            operating system version. This data is required to deliver the Website and
            to ensure its stability and security. The legal basis is our legitimate
            interest under Article 6(1)(f) GDPR. Netlify acts as a processor on our
            behalf under a data processing agreement; where data is transferred outside
            the EEA, the transfer is safeguarded by EU Standard Contractual Clauses.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Website Analytics (TelemetryDeck):</strong> We use TelemetryDeck to
            understand, in aggregate, how this Website is used — for example, how many
            people view a page or click a store badge. TelemetryDeck is privacy-focused
            and cookieless: it does not set cookies, does not store anything on your
            device, and does not create a persistent identifier that would allow you to
            be recognised across sessions or websites. Identifying elements are
            irreversibly hashed with a rotating salt before they are stored, so the
            resulting statistics cannot be traced back to an individual. Data is
            processed on servers in the European Union. The legal basis is our
            legitimate interest in measuring and improving our own website under
            Article 6(1)(f) GDPR.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>Fonts:</strong> The fonts used on this Website (Inter and
            Montserrat) are hosted on our own servers and delivered together with the
            page. No connection to Google Fonts or any other external font provider is
            established, and your IP address is therefore not transmitted to any font
            provider.
        </li>
        <li>
            <strong>No Advertising or Social Media Trackers:</strong> This Website does
            not embed advertising networks, social media plugins, remarketing pixels, or
            similar third-party tracking technologies.
        </li>
    </ul>

    <h3>Links to the App Store and Google Play</h3>
    <p>
        The download buttons on this Website link to the Apple App Store and the Google
        Play Store. These links carry campaign parameters that tell us which of our own
        marketing channels a download came from — Apple campaign tokens (<code
            >pt</code
        > and <code>ct</code>) for the App Store, and a referrer value containing UTM
        parameters (<code>utm_source</code>, <code>utm_medium</code>, <code
            >utm_campaign</code
        >) for Google Play.
    </p>
    <p>
        These parameters describe the link you clicked, not you. They contain no
        personal data, no identifier, and no information about your device, and nothing
        is stored on your device when the link is displayed or clicked. They are only
        transmitted once you actively click a button and are then evaluated in aggregate
        form in Apple's App Analytics and Google Play Console, so that we can see how
        many downloads originated from this Website. Once you follow such a link, you
        leave this Website and the privacy policy of Apple or Google applies to the
        further processing of your data. The legal basis for adding these parameters is
        our legitimate interest in measuring the effectiveness of our own marketing under
        Article 6(1)(f) GDPR.
    </p>

